li-xii-p2 = prose (cons "Two minds without ignorance do not disagree; a mind without ignorance does not enter conflict with one that has it, but holds it until the ignorance dissolves; only ignorance meets ignorance in conflict. Controversy (contra + versus) is a question turned between poles until it shows itself; consensus (con + sentire, perceiving together) is where the turning arrives; conflict is controversy stopped halfway. Collaborative intelligence is bounded by the mutual information between minds, and every substitution of an enforced word for an exact one narrows it. A mind, human or machine, that can learn another's code of language at the moment of contact widens the channel; one that enforces a standard register narrows it, and at the scale of a civilization, that narrowing is central control of thought." nil)
